WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:06.670 line:-3
Stop using it like Google.

2
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:21.920 line:-3
Everyone is using it. Few use it well. 64% of US teens use AI chatbots. 47% of student chats asked directly for an answer or finished work.

3
00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:37.470 line:-3
Nearly 1 000 pupils. Practice with AI: +48% and +127%. Exam, AI off: −17%. Practice soared. Learning sank.

4
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:53.180 line:-3
Design beats the chatbot. At Harvard, 194 physics students learnt from an AI tutor built around how people learn: the median gain was more than double. The software made students follow the steps in order.

5
00:00:54.630 --> 00:01:05.800 line:-3
Asked “Are you sure?”, one model wrongly admitted a “mistake” in up to 98% of challenged answers.

6
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:23.050 line:-3
Most AI tests give marks for a lucky guess, but none for “I don’t know”. An older model was wrong 75% of the time. A newer one skipped half the questions: wrong 26%.

7
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:32.970 line:-3
A legal team cited nine cases. Only two could be traced. The court: “irresponsible and downright unprofessional”.

8
00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:43.420 line:-3
Asked to explain 36 + 59, it described “carry the one”. That is not what it actually did.

9
00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:55.630 line:-3
Memory is the residue of thought. If the AI does the thinking, it is the AI’s “memory” that gets the practice, not yours.

10
00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:05.780 line:-3
Augment your thinking: explain, question, give feedback. Don’t automate it: write, solve, summarise for you.

11
00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:16.500 line:-3
Attempt it first. Name the blockage. Ask for ONE hint. Check it. Close the AI, go again.

12
00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:26.420 line:-3
The hint ladder: climb only as high as you need. The full solution is the last resort.

13
00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:40.470 line:-3
The most successful prompts average about 21 words. Most people type fewer than 9. A good prompt is a short paragraph, not a search.

14
00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:52.050 line:-3
UCT stopped using AI-detection scores: “simply not reliable”. Expect to explain your work out loud. Declare your AI use.

15
00:02:53.500 --> 00:03:05.330 line:-3
Brain On, AI On: AI is a power tool. Your brain is the power. Co-Pilot, Not Autopilot: you fly the plane. AI helps you navigate.

16
00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:14.320 line:-3
The measure that counts: what you can do with the AI switched off.
